docs/DECISIONS.md-988-

codex
**Do not send this candidate.** A fifth Stage A would be decision-moving if valid, but this particular send would spend most of the remaining budget on an unmeasured combination whose evidence does not justify making it the final configuration.

D439 delegates choices that would otherwise go to Alex, but [D426](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4721>) records his specific decision that no fifth Stage A is sent and remains in force. The later general delegation does not explicitly reverse that decision. A council decision to override it would need an explicit basis in Alex’s words; it should not be assumed from chronology alone. [D439](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4871>)

Independently of authority, sol with A2 plus v2 has never been measured as a pair. Astra’s A2 finding is descriptive from a voided reading and cannot establish the effect on sol. Sol’s unchanged-request comparison was inconclusive and had **5 agreed failures in 78**; its later screens add evidence, not a measurement of the proposed combination. [Sol result](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/model/RESULT.md>), [D640–D641](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:984>)

The $1.10 cost is an estimate, not proof that 132 answers and retries will finish within the remaining ceiling. An incomplete run would be **NOT MEASURED**.

I see **no supported in-authority, in-budget step on the present record that would move the production decision**. That is a conclusion about the candidates examined, not a claim that no future candidate can exist.

CONSENSUS: no, because the proposed fifth Stage A lacks an explicit reversal of D426 and a sufficiently validated final configuration.
